 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the education law, in relation to allowing students attending\nagricultural learning events to be recorded as in attendance at school",
    "basePrintNo": "S6655",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6655-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 45,
       "fullName": "Dan Stec",
       "imgName": "674_dan_stec.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1490,
       "sessionMemberId": 2362,
       "sessionYear": 2025,
       "shortName": "STEC"
      },
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 49,
       "fullName": "Mark Walczyk",
       "imgName": "1067_Mark_Walczyk.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1523,
       "sessionMemberId": 2366,
       "sessionYear": 2025,
       "shortName": "WALCZYK"
      }
     ],
     "size": 2
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §3207-b, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6655\n\nSPONSOR: GRIFFO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to allowing students\nattending agricultural learning events to be recorded as in attendance\nat school\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAllows students attending agricultural learning events to he counted as\nin attendance at school.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\n1. The education law is amended by adding a new section 3207-h to read\nas follows: School attendance for agricultural learning events. 1. A\nschool district may permit an enrolled student, with the consent of such\nstudent's parent, guardian, or other person in parental relation. to\nattend an agricultural learning event. For the purposes of attendance,\nany student so serving while school is in session shall be recorded as\nin attendance.\n\n2. For purposes of this section, an \"agricultural learning event- shall\ninclude. but not be limited to, scheduled event of state future farmers\nof America (FFA) associations. the national future farmers of America\n(FFA) organizations, and 4-H programs as part of organized competitions\nor exhibitions.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation mirrors HB 3814 passed by Illinois Governor .1B Pritzk-\ner in 2023 to allow students attending agricultural learning events such\nas FFA and 4-H programs to be credited as their participation towards\nschool attendance. New York State is a leader in the agricultural indus-\ntry, and to help ensure the growth of the industry, we must invest in\nour future generations of agricultural leaders. This legislation would\nencourage students involved in the FFA and 4-H to continue their partic-\nipation in the program while not be penalized for an unexcused absence\nfrom school.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2024- S.8107-Referred to Education Committee\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
